## Script Standards (this repo)

All reusable scripts must follow these conventions: setup, check/audit, installer, deploy, hooks, shell aliases.

### Block order (setup scripts)

**Bash:** shebang/header > `set -euo pipefail` > logging block (`ERRORS=0` + helpers) > OS guard > body > exit footer
**PS1:** header > logging block (`$errors = 0` + helpers) > OS guard > body > exit footer

### Error tracking (required)

- `log_error()` MUST do `ERRORS=$((ERRORS + 1))`
- `LogError` MUST do `$script:errors++`
- Missing tracking is a bug -- scripts silently exit 0 on failure.

### Logging helpers

Bash: `log`/`log_ok`/`log_error`/`log_warn`. PS1: `Log`/`LogOk`/`LogError`/`LogWarn`. UTC timestamps with Z suffix.

### Exit footer

Check error counter, exit 1 on failure, exit 0 on success. See gold standards: `scripts/setup-user-mcp.sh/.ps1`.

### Error handling (all scripts)

Every error-suppression pattern requires an immediate result check:

- `-ErrorAction SilentlyContinue` -- null/empty check within 3 lines
- `2>/dev/null`, `|| true` -- comment + result check
- `try/catch` -- catch must log or re-throw; empty `catch {}` is never OK

**Exception:** Command-existence checks (`Get-Command`, `command -v`) with explicit fallback.

**Anti-pattern:** Suppressed errors feeding into counts/loops with no null guard (false pass).

### Check/audit scripts

- `StepPass`/`StepFail`/`StepWarn` must handle internal errors
- `Get-ChildItem`/`Get-Content` failures -- `StepFail` or `StepWarn`, never silent skip
- Test file/directory existence before processing
- `StepPass` must accept `$Detail` parameter matching `StepFail`/`StepWarn`/`StepSkip`

### Post-write validation

Template-generated files: validate content correctness, not just structural markers.

### Exemptions

Intentional suppression without result check requires: header comment + entry in exemptions table in `.claude/rules/script-standards.md` (protected file, user approval needed).
